{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"bob-cli-gv:000001:issue_created:bob-cli-gv:83f18f4687cd570748752e0f405fab02ca188e77e489e99d64adc0d48bd3ad9e","timestamp":"2026-11-04T03:27:01Z","actor":"bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-gr.land","operation":"issue_created","issue_id":"bob-cli-gv","payload":{"kind":"issue_created","issue":{"id":"bob-cli-gv","title":"bob periods brief gives no count behind the Finished/Dropped cap, so drafts cannot write the callout's +N more","status":"open","issue_type":"task","parent_id":null,"owner":"bryanbugyi34@gmail.com","assignee":"","created_at":"2026-11-04T03:27:01Z","created_by":"bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-gr.land","updated_at":"2026-11-04T03:27:01Z","closed_at":null,"close_reason":null,"description":"","design":"","model":"","size":"small","task_type":"bug","task_type_fields":{"impact":"Every weekly Review either omits the +N more tail the callout requires or invents a basis for it.","location":"src/native/periods/brief.rs finished_section, dropped_section, render_finished","repro":"The weekly v1 callout asks for \"`^prj` completions first, then at most 7 tasks, then `+N more`\". `bob periods brief 2026-W43 -f md` prints at most 7 Finished rows and 7 Dropped rows but no count of what was cut. The Done fact can't stand in for that count: it excludes the daily `^gtd` rows that Finished includes. W31's vault has 51 completions against Done 48; W30 matched (55 vs 55). Drafters fell back to phrases like \"+more of 60 Done\" (W29).\n\nRoot cause: `finished_section` and `dropped_section` call `truncate(ctx.finish_cap)` without recording the pre-truncation length. The Done fact comes from the stats report on a different basis. Fix: emit `total` (and `more = total - shown`) for Finished and Dropped in JSON, and print `+N more` in `-f md`.\n"},"is_ready_to_work":false,"changespec_name":"","changespec_bug_id":"","creation_reason":"Proposed by bob-cli-gr.1 note #3 and corroborated by bob-cli-gr.11, gr.13, and gr.14: the callout asks drafters for a `+N more` count that the brief never provides.","dependencies":[]}}}
